# Who reviews what.
#
# This replaces the squad-named folders. The directories are now named after what
# they run — vote/, worker/, nginx/ — and ownership lives here instead, which is
# better than a folder name because GitHub acts on it: open a PR touching vote/ and
# Squad B is requested as reviewer automatically. That is the "pull requests with
# peer sign-off" the brief asks for, enforced rather than agreed.
#
# Last match wins, so the specific lines below override the catch-all.
# Replace the placeholder handles with real GitHub usernames before merging.

# Catch-all: the repo lead reviews anything not claimed below.
*                       @Miketopex

# Squad A — infrastructure
/infra/                 @Miketopex

# Squad B — vote service
/vote/                  @Anointed-Excel

# Squad C — worker and data
/worker/                @Miketopex

# Squad D — containers, nginx, deployment
/nginx/                 @Miketopex
/scripts/               @Miketopex
/docker-compose.yml     @Miketopex
/docker-compose.prod.yml @Miketopex

# Squad E — QA, monitoring and documentation
/qa/                    @Miketopex
/docs/                  @Miketopex
/README.md              @Miketopex

# CI/CD belongs to Squad D, but a change here affects everyone, so the lead sees it too.
/.github/               @Miketopex
